title: The Scientific Method in Everyday Life
subtitle: Ask, test, and revise with evidence
coverColor: #059669
objectives:
  - Design a fair test with one changed variable.
  - Distinguish observation from inference.

<<<Section>>>
title: Asking testable questions
subtitle: From wonder to hypothesis
themeColor: #F59E0B

<<<Lesson>>>
title: What makes a question testable

<<<Text markdown>>>
## Testable vs. interesting

"Why is the sky beautiful?" is interesting but not testable. "Does light color
change monggo growth in 7 days?" names variables, time, and a measure.
<<<Text/>>>

<<<Glossary>>>
- term: Variable
  definition: Anything that can change in an investigation.
- term: Control
  definition: The setup kept unchanged for comparison.
<<<Glossary/>>>

<<<Video>>>
youtubeUrl: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=abcdefghijk
title: Fair tests in 3 minutes
transcript: A narrator explains variables, controls, and one-change-at-a-time testing with a plant example.
<<<Video/>>>
